    693  f0cc							; --- Kernel-entry re-anchor (bugs.md #29 Class C, 2026-10-11) ---
    694  f0cc							; TIM64T expires on a 64-cycle tick, the poll exits up to 63c late, and
    695  f0cc							; the band-0 .Row setup WSYNC gap is ~75c — so the kernel start line
    696  f0cc							; oscillated ±1 with the tick phase (measured: first .Line WSYNC at scn
    697  f0cc							; 20 on 100 frames, scn 21 on 51 frames under bomb/thrust input = the
    698  f0cc							; whole-screen jitter, HUD seam flipping rows 144/194). The re-anchor
    699  f0cc							; below (VBLANK still on = blank line) absorbs the quantization: the
