   2528  f9b5							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2529  f9b5							; RefreshEnemyY moved post-pad (after TitleWork) — 2026-10-02, so its SELECT
   2530  f9b5							; → title check costs 0 pre-pad bytes (headroom 1B). Pins .ds $FBF8/$FC49
   2531  f9b5							; keep every downstream pre-pad address unchanged.
   2532  f9b5							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2533  f9b5
   2534  f9b5							; ==============================================================================
   2535  f9b5							; E4 moth exit tramp ($FC49-$FC4E) — bank2 executes `sta $1FF6` at $FC49
   2536  f9b5							; (byte-identical slice, guard: verify_build), then the fetch at $FC4C comes
   2537  f9b5							; from bank0 = `jmp UE_Next` (real label here — no cross-bank address sync).
   2538  f9b5							; bank0's `sta $1FF6` copy never runs; bank2's bytes from $FC4C never run.
   2539  f9b5							;
   2540  f9b5							; MUST stay off $FFF6-$FFF9: those are the ONLY addresses in code space where
   2541  f9b5							; (addr & $1FFF) lands in $1FF6-$1FF9 = F6 hotspot mirrors. Stella's
   2542  f9b5							; CartridgeEnhanced::peek (CartEnh.cxx:157, ADDR_MASK=$1FFF) calls
   2543  f9b5							; checkSwitchBank on READS — the old $FFF2 placement fetched the `jmp`
   2544  f9b5							; operands at $FFF6/$FFF7 and flipped banks mid-instruction (operand hi from
   2545  f9b5							; bank1 = $00 -> jmp $007D -> HUD runaway, 359/360-line frames, 5-byte stack
   2546  f9b5							; leak per rogue Overscan entry -> SP decayed to $E1 -> frame-3 crash where
   2547  f9b5							; jsr RefreshEnemyY's return landed on FetchPtr). Real F6 is write-only, but
   2548  f9b5							; no fetched byte may ever sit in the mirror zone.
   2549  f9b5							; ==============================================================================
   2550  f9b5							; ==============================================================================
   2551  f9b5							; Cross-bank call pads (docs/leaf_move_plan.md) — byte-identical copies live in
   2552  f9b5							; bank1 at the SAME addresses. F6 hotspots switch on ANY write — the written
   2553  f9b5							; value is ignored (proven by FoldIndirect's `sta $1FF6` carrying data bytes) —
   2554  f9b5							; so the pads `sta $1FF7`/`sta $1FF6` with A AS-IS: A/X/Y/flags pass through
   2555  f9b5							; unchanged, making the pad equivalent to the original inlined `jsr`.
   2556  f9b5							; (2026-09-30 bug: `lda #1` before `sta $1FF7` clobbered A — ClearPFColumn
   2557  f9b5							; punched col 1 instead of the bomb's col, AddScore added +1 instead of
   2558  f9b5							; +50/+75. Hole appeared at screen col 1 + mirror col 18 = "second tile from
   2559  f9b5							; each edge"; collision stayed correct because WallMask is separate.)
   2560  f9b5							; `sta` does not touch flags — IsRoomDark's `beq` contract survives the
   2561  f9b5							; return. Carry survives. No stack use.
   2562  f9b5							; ==============================================================================
   2563  f9b5		       00 00 00 	      .ds	$F9B8 - *, 0	; Phase 4 overlay tramp — shared address with
   2564  f9b8							; bank2's twin image (40B bank2 hole before
   2565  f9b8							; org $F9D9); F6-safe ($F9B1 & $1FFF ∉ hotspots)
   2566  f9b8				   OverlayTramp
   2567  f9b8		       a5 84		      lda	LineCount	; packed asym byte (0 = symmetric)
   2568  f9ba		       f0 03		      beq	.OTsym	; sym: clc/rts, never enters the cluster
   2569  f9bc		       4c 2d fa 	      jmp	PHMOverlay	; bank0 cluster ($FA30; repack chunk 4)
   2570  f9bf				   .OTsym
   2571  f9bf		       18		      clc
   2572  f9c0		       60		      rts
   2573  f9c1
   2574  f9c1							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2575  f9c1							; PositionBallM1 — D6 asymmetric objects, BOTH positioned in one VBL call.
   2576  f9c1							; WHY here: pre-pad headroom is 1B — inline ball+m1 (22B) cannot live in the
   2577  f9c1							; VBL block, so the ball block became this jsr and the body sits in the
   2578  f9c1							; $F9C4..$FBF7 fill (ReturnPad pin at $FBF8 unaffected; F6-safe:
   2579  f9c1							; $F9C4 & $1FFF = $19C4 ∉ $1FF6-$1FF9; bank0-only, not a fold twin).
   2580  f9c1							;   Temp	   = staged BallX (bank2 StageBandTab): 0 = symmetric → skip.
   2581  f9c1							;		     selector 4 = HMBL/RESPBL, ball x drawn clocks [A-7,A].
   2582  f9c1							;   CollisionEndX = staged M1X (MetaA nibble, bank2 StageBandTab):
   2583  f9c1							;		     0 = no M1 patch → skip.
   2584  f9c1							;		     selector 3 = HMM1/RESM1, left-col block x = 7+8*col
   2585  f9c1							;		     (passed to SetObjectXPos as M1X+1 — Stella draws 8-wide
   2586  f9c1							;		     M1 one clock left of the [A-7,A] player contract).
   2587  f9c1							;		     ENAM1 latched #$02 for the whole cave (hero-style: 2
   2588  f9c1							;		     ENAM writes/frame — enable here, clear in .AfterRows);
   2589  f9c1							;		     walls hide the parked M1 in unpatched bands (PF > M1 in
   2590  f9c1							;		     the priority chain — convert enforces the solid cell).
   2591  f9c1							; Runs before the single HMOVE (HMP0+X shadow registers accumulate).
   2592  f9c1							; Sym path cost: jsr+rts overhead only — no RESP/HMP write, frames stay
   2593  f9c1							; bit-identical to the pre-D6 build.
   2594  f9c1							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
